{"name":"Passion Flower","hex":"#6f5698","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"passion flower","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of passionflower."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/passion_flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Passion Flower (1930 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Passion Flower is a 1930 American pre-Code drama film directed and produced by William C. deMille and starring Kay Francis, Kay Johnson and Charles Bickford in a romantic triangle. This production includes actor Ray Milland's American screen debut, although his appearance as a party guest is uncredited."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Passion_Flower_%281930_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passion_Flower_(1930_film)","wikidata":"Q2056045"},{"title":"Passiflora","blocks":[{"text":"Passiflora, known also as the passion flowers or passion vines, is a genus of about 550 species of flowering plants, and the type genus of the family Passifloraceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/OQ_Passion_flower.jpg/330px-OQ_Passion_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passiflora","wikidata":"Q161185"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_g